inted in large, arched, bold, deep-purple capital letters. Directly below this is a stylized graphic of a grape bunch composed of overlapping deep-purple circles, each with a small white crescent highlight, topped by a single dark-green leaf and stem. To the left of the grapes, the words \\\"Prebiotics,\\\" \\\"Botanicals,\\\" and \\\"Plant Fiber\\\" are stacked vertically in a small, dark-green, sans-serif font, while to the right sits a circular dark-green \\\"Plant Powered / Microbiome Approved\\\" seal. Below the grape graphic, the flavor \\\"Classic Grape\\\" is written in a prominent, stacked, dark-green serif font, followed by the tagline \\\"A New Kind of Soda™\\\" in medium-purple sans-serif, with the volume \\\"12 fl oz (355 mL)\\\" centered at the very bottom. The lower-left flank displays \\\"Non GMO\\\" and the lower-right displays \\\"5g of sugar per can\\\" in matching medium-purple text, while the upper shoulder of the can reads \\\"Supports Digestive Health\\\" in small, dark-green block capitals. A variant design is also shown in some contexts, featuring a deep violet-purple can body with white lettering, white highlights on the grapes, and a lowercase \\\"classic grape\\\" flavor label.\\n\\nUse the product appearance text only as a private visual reference for accurately drawing the product. Do not print, quote, paraphrase, label, or turn any of that description into ad copy. Treat orientation-specific details carefully: show front-only details only when the product front is visible; if the brief shows the back, side, top, or an angled view where those details would not be visible, omit them instead of moving them onto the wrong face.\\n\\nThe attached product photos show the real product — reproduce it faithfully.\\n\\nThe final attached image is the official brand logo. Add it once, subtly, in clean negative space; keep it exact, legible, and uncropped.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n